  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: pca_n2000 as RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (0.635–0.639 vs. 0.512–0.542), making it the dominant design choice. However, with scgpt, rna_only (config_044, acc 0.530) was competitive with or slightly better than multimodal variants (0.512–0.542), suggesting the image branch may not add value. We have no rna_only data point with pca_n2000. Question: Does the image modality actually contribute when paired with the much stronger pca_n2000 encoder? config_042 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation against config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted), differing only in the presence of the image branch. Why best: The answer fundamentally redirects the remaining budget—if rna_only matches ~0.64, the image modality is dispensable and we can concentrate on RNA encoder/aggregation choices; if it drops substantially, multimodal fusion and image encoder selection become high-priority. This reduces the most consequential uncertainty before committing further experiments to multimodal variants."
}

